#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Leaf physiological response reconstruction: coupled Farquhar(C3)/Collatz(C4)
photosynthesis + Ball-Berry stomatal conductance, land-surface (CLM/Noah-MP)
convention.

Convention decisions fixed with the researcher (plan handoff):
  * pathway is the SINGLE global field leaf_params["pathway"] -> applied to the
    sunlit stream, the shaded stream AND all test cases.  Here it is "C4", so
    the C3 branch below is DORMANT (kept behind the same switch; it cannot touch
    any output for this dataset).
  * capacity: Vcmax(T) = vcmax25 * fT(T) * n_factor * btran  (CLM/Noah-MP fT
    incl. high-T inhibition).  Rd = 0.015 * that same scaled Vcmax object.
    The C4 Wj term alpha_q*APAR is NOT scaled (quantum yield is not capacity).
    The Ball-Berry intercept b0 is NOT scaled by btran.
  * night branch iff PAR <= 0 (literal rule, no ad hoc threshold).  Night:
    A = -Rd, gs = b0 exactly, with cs and Ci still closed through the diffusion
    chain (hence cs > ca and Ci > cs at night).
  * esat(T): CLM/Buck over water,
    esat = 611.21*exp((18.678 - Tc/234.5) * Tc/(257.14 + Tc)) [Pa], Tc in degC.
    R = 8.314 J mol-1 K-1.
  * rb_sm is already s/m and enters only as 1.37*rb (cs drawdown); 1.65*rs for
    Ci; gs is the water-vapour conductance with rs = cf/gs.
  * ca = co2_pa at face value (64.0646 Pa here).

n_iterations convention: the index k of the closure evaluation at which the
convergence test (|Ci_new - Ci| < TOL and |residual| < TOL, both in Pa) FIRST
succeeds, counting the evaluation at the supplied ci_init_pa as k = 1.  It is
therefore "number of coupled closure evaluations from the given start" and
equals (updates applied + 1); night rows = 1 because they need no iteration.
The convention is fixed and identical for all five cases, so the reported
differences reflect only how far each start guess lies from the common root.
"""

